@startuml enrol
!theme plain
title Enrolment: a person enrols a subscription once, through the vendor's own flow; the material lands only in the broker's store

actor "Person" as P
participant "Phone app / operator device key\nsecure element; biometric presence" as Phone
participant "claude CLI\n(vendor flow)" as V
participant "Operator command\nswarma-operator; no harness or shell\nbinary / wire format unpublished" as C
participant "Broker daemon\n(service user swarma-credential-broker)" as B
participant "Approved Codex executable\n(pinned digest, run by the broker)" as X
database "Secret store\n(0600 files, broker user)" as S

note over P,C
  For each enrolment: authentication plus exact content confirmation;
  widening refused from inside an agent session (§14).
  Phone enrolment, rotation and loss remain open (§18.15).
end note

== Authenticate and confirm each enrolment act ==
alt Phone-first path
  P -> Phone: inspect exact act (who, actions, until); biometric confirmation
  Phone -> Phone: sign canonical operator record; private key never leaves phone
  Phone -> C: SSH over tailnet, pinned key only; forced operator command; signed act
  C -> C: verify pinned phone signature bound to this exact act
else Terminal fallback (phone not required)
  P -> C: password-authenticated sudo into swarma-operator; confirm exact content
  C -> C: timestamp_timeout=0; no NOPASSWD or cached ticket
end
note over C,B
  Each enrolment below repeats this admission; account owner is swarma-operator.
  Operator-record domain/canonical bytes and transport mapping unpublished.
  Phone record is separate from existing broker envelopes (§4.3, §18.15).
end note

== Claude subscription ==
P -> V: claude setup-token (browser login)
V --> P: one-year token (printed, not stored)
P -> C: admitted enrolment act: curator broker enrol claude_code --account owner/claude/personal --token-stdin [--issued-at]
C -> B: connect; check the server's peer UID is the broker's
C -> B: hello; account.enrol {kind: claude-oauth-token, material}
B -> B: peer principal from kernel: swarma-operator (account owner)
B -> S: put(material) (atomic replace)
B --> C: account/1 {state: active, expires_at: computed | null}

== Codex personal plan: enrolment ceremony ==
P -> C: admitted enrolment act: curator broker enrol codex_cli --account owner/codex/personal
C -> B: account.enrol {kind: codex-chatgpt}
B -> B: confirm previous writer absence; unresolved rotation requires explicit re-enrolment (§9.4);\ncreate a fresh Codex home in the broker store\n(file credential storage, sanitised environment)
B -> X: start the vendor's device login in that home;\nv1: explicit proxy configuration for executable and network-using children
X --> B: verification address + code
B --> C: verification address + code
C --> P: open the address, enter the code
P -> P: completes the login in a browser
X --> B: login stored in the broker-owned home
B -> B: read the vendor account id;\nrefuse if another broker account maps to it (account_duplicate)
B --> C: account/1 {state: active}; auth owner started
note over B: no existing login is imported,\nno other home adopted, no keyring item exported;\nre-enrolment cannot bypass unresolved previous writer (§9.4)
note over B,X
  R-SVC-EGRESS v1: login/refresh/policy-fetch network only through
  dedicated broker proxy; observed endpoints and no direct fallback
  require qualification; local resolver bypass must be denied (§15.2).
  Person's browser runs under the person's account, outside broker egress.
  Proxy outage cannot permit direct login fallback.
  R-FATE fate table: user manager §7; previous-writer fence unchanged.
  R-LOCK releases state lock for cross-service I/O (§13.1).
end note
@enduml
